alue \\\"330\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R17 0 Net-_LED5-K_ 330k\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"LED5 is effectively off or extremely dim, so the FCC status indication is lost. The rest of the board is unaffected.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"NAVC1\", \"FCC1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"NAVC1.19\", \"NAVC1.32\", \"NAVC1.48\", \"NAVC1.64\", \"NAVC1.18\", \"NAVC1.63\", \"FCC1.11\", \"FCC1.27\", \"FCC1.50\", \"FCC1.75\", \"FCC1.100\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\", \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\", \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"Several supply pins of both MCUs are on single-pin 'unconnected' nets. NAVC1 VDD pins 19, 32, 48 and 64 and FCC1 VDD pins 11, 27, 50, 75 and 100 are not on +3V3. NAVC1 VSS pins 18 and 63 form their own net and are not on GND.\",\n      \"expected\": \"All VDD pins of both STM32 devices should be on the +3V3 rail, and all VSS pins on GND, as the spec states the 3V3 rail feeds both MCUs.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"276\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"92\\\") (name \\\"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If these are real connections missing from the board, the MCUs would be unpowered or have floating supply pins. This could be an artefact of how the netlist was exported, so confidence is low.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The most likely deviation is the PCA9685 address pin A0 strapped to +3.3V instead of GND, which moves the driver off its specified 0x40 address. LED5's 330k series resistor is also out of line with the other indicator LEDs.\"\n}",
